        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Though some ways of punctuating the end of a sentence are flat-out wrong, you can choose from among many that are right, and each has a different effect. If you look again at that passage by Mary Wollstonecraft about the waterfall (p. 154), you can see those choices in contrast.",
